AUDIO: 'These days, more software developers than ever are orchestrating AI agent swarms and stacking tool calls. But, here\'s the problem. Your context window fills up fast and hallucinations compound. If you aren\'t optimizing your tokens and validating your outputs, your agents might break. Benchmarks and'

[00:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'research across multiple AI models has suggested that the longer your inputs, the more unreliable the performance of the models become, even on relatively simple tasks. And that\'s why the tools that your AI agents and applications'

[00:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'call need to return information with a high signal-to-noise ratio, giving context without adding unnecessary load and overhead. Using a tool like SerpApi that grabs real-time search results can ground your application with more'

[00:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'relevant, localized data, and most importantly, fresh information that\'s newer than the model\'s training cutoff date. Previously, SerpApi returned structured data in only JSON format, but we listened to the needs of our users,'

[00:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and now you have the option of receiving the same results in markdown. The output in markdown contains the same information as our default JSON [music] output, but in a much more efficient data format. Our benchmarks show that on'

[01:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'average, you save about 50% of the tokens if you use markdown compared to JSON, and up to 90% for some APIs. Not only can this directly reduce the cost of your API calls because it uses fewer input tokens, the output also won\'t use'

[01:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'up so much of your AI\'s precious context window. This obviously means extra room for more examples, more conversational history, and retrieve documents in a rag pipeline. This makes your AI smarter by'

[01:30] [scene:talk]
